# 📘 Responsive Design (Media Queries)

---

## 1. Introduction to Responsive Design

Responsive design ensures websites adapt to different screen sizes (mobile, tablet, desktop).

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<style>
body { font-family: Arial; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Responsive Page</h1>
</body>
</html>
```

---

## 2. Media Query Basics

Media queries apply styles based on screen size.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<style>
body { background: lightblue; }

@media (max-width: 600px) {
  body { background: lightcoral; }
}
</style>
</head>
<body></body>
</html>
```

---

## 3. Breakpoints

Breakpoints define where layout changes.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<style>
.box { width: 100%; background: blue; }

@media (min-width: 768px) {
  .box { background: green; }
}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="box">Resize me</div>
</body>
</html>
```

---

## 4. Mobile First Design

Start designing for small screens, then scale up.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<style>
.box { background: red; }

@media (min-width: 768px) {
  .box { background: blue; }
}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="box">Mobile First</div>
</body>
</html>
```

---

## 5. max-width vs min-width

* `max-width` → applies to smaller screens
* `min-width` → applies to larger screens

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<style>
body { background: yellow; }

@media (max-width: 600px) {
  body { background: pink; }
}

@media (min-width: 800px) {
  body { background: lightgreen; }
}
</style>
</head>
<body></body>
</html>
```

---

## 6. Responsive Typography

Adjust font sizes for different devices.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<style>
h1 { font-size: 20px; }

@media (min-width: 768px) {
  h1 { font-size: 40px; }
}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Responsive Text</h1>
</body>
</html>
```

---

## 7. Responsive Layout with Flexbox

Change layout direction based on screen size.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<style>
.container {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
}

@media (min-width: 768px) {
  .container {
    flex-direction: row;
  }
}

.box {
  padding: 20px;
  background: lightblue;
  margin: 5px;
}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="container">
  <div class="box">1</div>
  <div class="box">2</div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

---

## 8. Responsive Grid Layout

Use Grid and adjust columns responsively.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<style>
.container {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr;
}

@media (min-width: 768px) {
  .container {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
  }
}

.box {
  background: orange;
  padding: 20px;
}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="container">
  <div class="box">1</div>
  <div class="box">2</div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

---

## 9. Hiding Elements Responsively

Show/hide content based on device size.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<style>
.mobile { display: block; }
.desktop { display: none; }

@media (min-width: 768px) {
  .mobile { display: none; }
  .desktop { display: block; }
}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="mobile">Mobile View</div>
<div class="desktop">Desktop View</div>
</body>
</html>
```

---

## 10. Responsive Images

Make images scale with screen size.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<style>
img {
  max-width: 100%;
  height: auto;
}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<img src="https://via.placeholder.com/600">
</body>
</html>
```

---

# 🎯 Summary

* Media queries control layout based on screen size
* `min-width` = mobile-first scaling up
* `max-width` = desktop-first scaling down
* Combine with Flexbox/Grid for powerful layouts
* Use responsive units and images for full adaptability